.TH CHANGELOG-GENERATE 8 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
changelog generate \- regenerate changelog from stored metadata and fragments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changelog generate
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIVERSION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBgenerate\fR command regenerates the full changelog file from stored fragment data and metadata. Unlike \fBreleaserelease\fR which creates individual version entries, \fBgenerate\fR produces a complete CHANGELOG.md with all historical versions in reverse chronological order.

This is useful for:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Rebuilding the changelog after configuration changes
.IP \(bu 2
Regenerating after fragment modifications or additions
.IP \(bu 2
Creating fresh changelogs from .changes.yaml metadata files
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.

.TP
.B Positional Arguments:
.TP
\fIVERSION\fR
Specific version to generate (e.g., "v1.0.0"). If omitted, generates the complete changelog with all versions.

.TP
.B Optional Flags:
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dir\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Changelog base directory containing fragments/. Defaults to current directory's \fIchangelogs/\fR subdirectory.

.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-notes-dir\fR=\fIDIR\fR
Additional fragment directories to merge into the output. Can be specified multiple times.

.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Output file path for the generated changelog. Defaults to "CHANGELOG.md" in the current directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-only-latest\fR
Only write the changelog entry for the latest version, without preamble of historical entries. Useful for incremental updates or when combined with \fB\-\-output\fR for targeted regeneration.

.TP
\fB\-\-reload\-plugins\fR
Force reload of plugin cache during generation.

.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\fR
Update existing entries from fragments and refresh plugin descriptions.

.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-plugins\fR=\fIMODE\fR
Specify how to handle plugin description updates: "allow-removal" or "prevent-removal".

.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-fragments\fR=\fIMODE\fR
Control which fragments to include: "without-archives" (default) or "with-archives".

.TP
\fB\-\-collection\-namespace\fR=\fINAMESPACE\fR
Override the collection namespace for Ansible-style projects.

.TP
\fB\-\-collection\-name\fR=\fINAME\fR
Override the collection name.

.TP
\fB\-\-collection\-flatmap\fR
Enable flat mapping using short plugin names instead of fully qualified names.

.TP
\fB\-\-is\-collection\fR=\fIBOOL\fR
Override whether this is a collection project (true/false/yes/no).

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-semantic\-versioning\fR
Disable semantic versioning enforcement for this generation.
.SH GENERATION PROCESS
.PP
The generate command:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Reads all fragment files from main and notes directories
.IP \(bu 2
Loads existing .changes.yaml metadata if present
.IP \(bu 2
Processes fragments according to category priority and date sorting
.IP \(bu 2
Generates version entries with proper headers and formatting
.IP \(bu 2
Writes complete changelog file with all versions in reverse chronological order
.RE

.TP
.B Output Structure:
.nf
    # Changelog
    All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

    ## [v1.0.0] - 2026-07-29
    ### Breaking Changes / Porting Guide
    * **PG-001**: Fixed crash when processing large files.

    ### Bugfixes
    * **IMP-456**: Added support for parallel processing.

    ## [v0.9.0] - 2026-06-15
    ... historical entries continue in reverse chronological order
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate complete changelog with all versions:
.nf
    changelog generate
.fi

.TP
Generate only the latest version entry:
.nf
    changelog generate --only-latest --output CHANGELOG.md
.fi

.TP
Regenerate for a specific version:
.nf
    changelog generate v1.2.0 --output releases/v1.2.0.md
.fi

.TP
Generate with custom notes directories:
.nf
    changelog generate \\
        -n changelogs/fragments/core \\
        -n changelogs/notes/community \\
        -o CHANGELOG.full.md
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
\fBchangelog-release(8)\fR \- Generate individual release entries from fragments
.TP
\fBchangelog-add(8)\fR \- Create new fragment files
.TP
\fBchangelog-config(5)\fR \- Configuration file reference
